{
  "id": "c04",
  "subject": "build: integrate a prebuilt external QEMU (drop the QEMU submodule)",
  "body_points": [
    "QEMU_BIN_DIR in config.env points at an externally built qemu-system-* dir; setup.sh validates it; plugins build out-of-tree against a vendored qemu-plugin.h, no QEMU source needed"
  ],
  "construct": "git rm the QEMU gitlink + .gitmodules entry + scripts/build_qemu.sh. Add qemu_plugin/include/qemu-plugin.h (final version) + final qemu_plugin/Makefile adapted to this stage. Rewrite setup.sh for the external-QEMU flow (target the FINAL setup.sh minus vsim-external minus rv32 qemu32 lookup). config.env.example gains QEMU_BIN_DIR + HYBRID_TOOLCHAIN. Create untracked WT/config.env from the env block so later validations work.",
  "validate": [
    "make -C qemu_plugin (must produce libhybrid_handoff.so)",
    "bash -n setup.sh"
  ]
}
